  "narrative": {
    "benchmark_md": "Against the engagement-locked peer set (Rule R7) \u2014 Pershing Square Capital Management, Third Point LLC, Starboard Value LP, ValueAct Capital and Millennium Management \u2014 Elliott scores above the peer median in all four pillars and in 16 of 17 categories. The four activist peers cluster as P1-strong (governance/strategy 3.0-3.5) and P2-servicing-light (CRM-less, 1.8-2.5). Millennium Management is the lead competitor and the multi-manager outlier: its P3 Automation (4.0) and P4 Analytics/Architecture (4.0) reflect a Google Cloud platform with Vertex AI and BigQuery serving 300+ investment teams and ~1,200 technologists (re-validated June 2026), and it is the bar Elliott's enterprise data and AI estate trails. Starboard Value is the direct precedent that Salesforce can be an activist target \u2014 reinforcing that Elliott's relationship with Salesforce is as an investor (Jesse Cohn's 2023 stake, E-058), not a user. The implication: Elliott's P2 servicing and personalization opportunity is a leapfrog (peers are equally CRM-less), while its P4 data and AI opportunity is competitive catch-up to Millennium's bar.",
